{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q1075665","formula":"Mg(UO₂)₂(SiO₃OH)₂·6H₂O","hill":"H14MgO18Si2U2","elements":["H","O","Mg","Si","U"],"composition":{"H":14.0,"O":18.0,"U":2.0,"Mg":1.0,"Si":2.0},"names":{"en":"Sklodowskite","ru":"Склодовскит","uk":"Склодовськіт"},"descriptions":{"en":"Sklodowskite is a uranium mineral with the chemical formula: Mg(UO2)2(HSiO4)2·5H2O. It is a secondary mineral which contains magnesium and is a bright yellow colour, its crystal habit is acicular, but can form in other shapes. It has a Mohs hardness of about 2–3. It is named after the maiden name of Marie Skłodowska Curie.","uk":"Склодовськіт — мінерал урану з хімічною формулою: Mg(UO2)2(HSiO4)2·5H2O. Це вторинний мінерал, який містить магній і має яскраво-жовтий колір, його кристал має голчасту форму, але може мати й інші форми. Склодовськіт має твердість за шкалою Мооса приблизно 2-3. Названий на честь Марії Склодовської-Кюрі."},"fame":13,"pubchemCid":null,"mass":null,"charge":0,"smiles":null,"inchikey":null,"iupac":null,"classes":[{"qid":"Q12089225","names":{"en":"mineral species","ru":"действительный вид минералов","uk":"мінеральний вид"}}],"structureInfo":null,"structure":null,"sources":[{"role":"identity","name":"Wikidata","url":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q1075665","license":"CC0 1.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (en)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sklodowskite","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (uk)","url":"https://uk.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D0%A1%D0%BA%D0%BB%D0%BE%D0%B4%D0%BE%D0%B2%D1%81%D1%8C%D0%BA%D1%96%D1%82","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"role":"photo","name":"Wikimedia Commons","url":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sklodowskite-Gypsum-176753.jpg","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0"}],"similar":[{"id":"Q2479128","formula":"Cu(UO₂)₂(SiO₃OH)₂·6H₂O","names":{"en":"Cuprosklodowskite","uk":"Купросклодовськіт"},"elements":["H","O","Si","Cu","U"],"fame":14,"kind":null},{"id":"Q423494","formula":"Ca(UO₂)₂(SiO₃OH)₂·5H₂O","names":{"en":